silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_concrete_anchor#transportpushforward a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.03_pullback_vs_pushforward.sections.01_pushforward_as_information_flow.concrete_anchor#transportpushforward" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_concrete_anchor#transportpushforward silm:hasLongDescription "The TransportPushforward is the pushforward of the Vet-Imports-Household-Records functor. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F_*', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_concrete_anchor#transportpullback a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.20_functorial_transport.chapters.03_pullback_vs_pushforward.sections.01_pushforward_as_information_flow.concrete_anchor#transportpullback" .
silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_concrete_anchor#transportpullback silm:hasLongDescription "The TransportPullback is the pullback functor (sec 02). The bare math anchor-node name is resolved to a concrete household-or-clinic node of the Mittens vet-clinic transport scenario so a zero-math reader can ground the reading; the transport functor F preserves the typed arrows that bind this node into the larger commutative diagram." .
