silm:instances_papers_20_functorial_transport_chapters_03_pullback_vs_pushforward_sections_01_pushforward_as_information_flow_concrete_anchor#derivedanchor_01_pus_3 silm:hasLongDescription "The DerivedAnchor_01_pus_3 is a derived anchor for the transport diagram: the clinic-side image of the household typed leg, carrying composition data. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'DerivedAnchor_3', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
